# Home Assistant App: RustDesk Server

[![GitHub Release][releases-shield]][releases]
[![License][license-shield]][license]

Self-hosted [RustDesk][rustdesk] server (`hbbs` + `hbbr`) for your own
remote-desktop relay.

## About

This Home Assistant App (formerly add-on) lets you self-host the signaling
(`hbbs`) and relay (`hbbr`) services required by RustDesk clients. It bundles
the free, open-source RustDesk Server rather than RustDesk Server Pro.

For installation, configuration, external access, Tailscale, NGINX Streams,
Cloudflare, and troubleshooting guidance, see the full
[App documentation][docs].

## Maintenance

RustDesk, the Home Assistant base image, and workflow dependencies are monitored
with Renovate. CI builds both supported architectures, verifies upstream
RustDesk download digests, and scans the resulting App images before merge.

## Support

- [Open an issue on GitHub][issues] for reproducible App bugs.
- [Home Assistant community thread][forum] for setup and networking discussion.
- [Security policy][security] for sensitive reports.

